//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ VIP Shop of the IGC Client, opened with the VIP Shop icon of the HUD, the Cash Shop stays as it is and works next to it
//~~ Edit the file with Tools\IGC.VipShopEditor\VipShopEditor.html, reload it with the Game Server console command data.reload.vipshop
//~~ Prices are calculated by the Game Server, bought items wait in the shop storage until the player claims them
//~~ Times: yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm, server local time, empty for no limit
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### VipShop ###
//	Enabled: Whether or not, activate the VIP Shop, 0/1
//	Currency: Name of the currency shown next to prices, the balance is always WCoin
//	TopUpUrl: Payment page opened by the Top-up tab, {account} is replaced by the account ID and {pack} by TopUp::Pack ID, write & as &amp;
//	NewTabs: Tabs with a NEW badge, list of Vip, Shop, TopUp, Packages separated by comma
//	FooterNote: First line of the window footer
//	RequestCooldownMs: Minimum time between two shop requests of a player, milliseconds
//	MaxGiftMessage: Maximum length of a gift message, 0-60
//	GiftMinLevel: Character level required to send a gift, 0 for any level
//	GiftMinTopUp: WCoin the account must have topped up in total before it can send a gift, 0 to disable
//
// ### VipShop::Tabs ###
//	Vip: Whether or not, show the VIP tab, 0/1
//	Shop: Whether or not, show the item shop tab, 0/1
//	TopUp: Whether or not, show the top-up tab, 0/1
//	Packages: Whether or not, show the packages tab, 0/1
//
// ### VipShop::PriceTables::Table ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the price table, 1-255
//	Levels: Price of item level +0 to +15, 16 values separated by comma
//	Skill: Price of the skill
//	Luck: Price of the luck
//	OptionStep: Price of every +4 of the additional option
//	Excellent: Price of every excellent option
//	Socket: Price of every socket
//	Ancient5: Price of the +5 ancient option
//	Ancient10: Price of the +10 ancient option
//
// ### VipShop::PriceTables::Table::Duration ###
//	Days: Item duration sold with the table, 0-3650 days, 0 for permanent
//	Percent: Price of the duration, percent of the price of a permanent item
//
// ### VipShop::Categories::Category ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the item category, 1-255, categories are shown in this order
//	Name: Name of the category
//
// ### VipShop::Vip::Tier ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the VIP tier
//	VipType: VIP type sold, see VIPSystem.xml
//	Name: Name of the tier
//	Look: Look of the tier card: bronze, silver, gold, platinum
//	Hero: Whether or not, show the tier as the big banner, 0/1, one tier only
//
// ### VipShop::Vip::Tier::Offer ###
//	Days: VIP days sold
//	Price: Price of the offer, 0 requires Free set to 1
//	OldPrice: Former price shown crossed out, 0 for none
//	Free: Whether or not, the offer is free on purpose, 0/1, optional
//
// ### VipShop::Vip::Tier::Perk ###
//	Text: One line of the tier description
//
// ### VipShop::Items::Item ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the item offer, 1-65535
//	Category: ID of the category, see VipShop::Categories
//	Group: Category of the item, refer to ItemList.xml
//	Index: Index of the item, refer to ItemList.xml
//	BasePrice: Base price of the item, 0 requires Free set to 1
//	Free: Whether or not, the item is free on purpose, 0/1, optional
//	PriceTable: ID of the price table, see VipShop::PriceTables
//	Tag: Badge of the offer: Hot, New, Sale, empty for none
//	Discount: Discount of the final price, 0-99 percent
//	Level: Item levels the player can choose, range, e.g. 0-15
//	Option: Additional option steps the player can choose, range, 0-7 (+0 to +28), equipment only
//	Skill: Whether or not, the player can add the skill, 0/1, items with skill only
//	Luck: Whether or not, the player can add the luck, 0/1, equipment only
//	Sockets: Maximum number of sockets the player can choose, socket items only, 1-5, 1-3 on socket accessories, 0 for none
//	Ancient: Ancient options the player can choose: 0 for none, 5, 10 or 5,10, set items only, not together with sockets
//	Excellent: Excellent options the player can choose, Number of ExcellentOptions.xml separated by comma, empty for none
//		~ 0-5: Regular excellent options
//		~ 6 and above: Extended excellent options, maximum 3 on an item
//
//	MaxExcellent: Maximum number of excellent options the player can choose
//	Counts: Stack sizes sold, separated by comma, stackable items only
//	Durations: Durations sold, Days of the price table separated by comma, 0 for permanent
//	LimitCount: Number of purchases per account within LimitPeriod, 0 for no limit
//	LimitPeriod: Period of LimitCount: None, Day, Week (from Monday), Month, Total, Sale (from Start to End)
//	Stock: Number of items sold on the whole server, 0 for no limit
//	Start: Start of the sale
//	End: End of the sale
//	Description: Description line of the offer
//	Giftable: Whether or not, the item can be bought as a gift, 0/1
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ An item cannot have ancient and excellent options together
//~~ Price: (BasePrice + Levels of the level + Skill + Luck + OptionStep * option + Excellent * options + Socket * sockets + Ancient5 or Ancient10)
//~~ * Percent of the duration / 100 * count * (100 - Discount) / 100, rounded down, up to 2,000,000,000
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### VipShop::Packages::Package ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the package
//	Name: Name of the package, also the title in the shop storage, up to 40 characters
//	Description: Description line of the package
//	Filter: Text of the filter button the package is listed under, e.g. Starter, Growth
//	Price: Price of the package, 0 requires Free set to 1
//	Free: Whether or not, the package is free on purpose, 0/1, optional
//	ForSale: Whether or not, the package is sold, 0 for a package given only by a coupon, 0/1, optional, 1 by default
//	OldPrice: Former price shown crossed out, 0 for none
//	Tag: Badge of the package: Hot, New, Sale, empty for none
//	Flash: Whether or not, show the package in the flash sale banner with a countdown, 0/1, requires End
//	LimitCount: Number of purchases per account within LimitPeriod, 0 for no limit
//	LimitPeriod: Period of LimitCount: None, Day, Week (from Monday), Month, Total, Sale (from Start to End)
//	Stock: Number of packages sold on the whole server, 0 for no limit
//	Start: Start of the sale
//	End: End of the sale
//	Giftable: Whether or not, the package can be bought as a gift, 0/1
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ A sold package whose Coins are equal to or above its lowest price (daily deal price included) is not loaded
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### VipShop::Packages::Package::Item ###
//	Group: Category of the item, refer to ItemList.xml
//	Index: Index of the item, refer to ItemList.xml
//	Level: Level of the item, 0-15, optional
//	Skill: Item with skill, 0/1, optional
//	Luck: Item with luck, 0/1, optional
//	Option: Additional option, 0-7, optional
//	Excellent: Excellent options, Number of ExcellentOptions.xml separated by comma, optional
//	Ancient: Ancient option, 0, 5 or 10, optional
//	Sockets: Number of sockets, optional
//	Element: Element of a Pentagram, 1-5, optional
//	Count: Stack size or durability, optional
//	Days: Item duration in days, 0 for permanent, optional
//
// ### VipShop::Packages::Package::Vip ###
//	VipType: VIP type given, see VIPSystem.xml
//	Days: VIP days given
//
// ### VipShop::Packages::Package::Coins ###
//	Amount: WCoin given when the player claims the package
//
// ### VipShop::DailyDeal ###
//	Discount: Discount of the package of the day, percent
//	Pool: IDs of the packages separated by comma, one package per day in turn, changing at midnight server time
//
// ### VipShop::TopUp ###
//	FirstBonusPercent: Extra WCoin of the first top-up of an account, percent
//	PaymentTypes: Payment methods shown in the window, separated by comma
//
// ### VipShop::TopUp::Pack ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the pack, sent to TopUpUrl as {pack}
//	Coins: WCoin of the pack
//	Bonus: Bonus WCoin of the pack
//	Price: Price of the pack in real money, for the payment website
//	PriceLabel: Text of the pack button
//	Badge: Badge of the pack: Popular, Best, empty for none
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ WCoin are added by the payment website: one row per payment in the IGC_VipShop_TopUp table (MuOnline database)
//~~ with AccountID, PackId, Coins (Coins and Bonus of the pack), a unique Reference of the payment and ProcessedAt left empty (NULL)
//~~ The Data Server adds the WCoin within about 10 seconds and sets ProcessedAt
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### VipShop::TopUp::Monthly ###
//	Need: WCoin topped up in the current month to claim the reward, every reward can be claimed once a month, maximum 32 rewards
//	Name: Name of the reward
//	Item, Vip, Coins: What the reward gives, same settings as in VipShop::Packages::Package
//
// ### VipShop::ServerCoupons::Coupon ###
//	Code: Coupon code, 1-20 characters A-Z 0-9 _ -, not case sensitive
//	Coins: WCoin given by the coupon, 0 for none
//	PackageID: ID of the package given by the coupon, 0 for none
//	MaxUses: Number of uses on the whole server, 0 for no limit
//	PerAccount: Number of uses per account, must be 1
//	Start: Start of the coupon
//	End: End of the coupon
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Coupons are never sent to the game client, keep this file where players cannot read it
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

